  "notes": "Source: Mercy University official Academic Program Sequence Map, 'Bachelor of Science in Computer Science', Catalog Year 2026-2027 (https://www.mercy.edu/media/20262027-bs-computer-science; Office of the Provost, April 2026). Degree name verified: 'Bachelor of Science in Computer Science' (map heading). Transcription method: manual verbatim transcription of the official term-by-term sequence map on 2026-09-30; course titles use the map's wording (Mercy's own abbreviated catalog style, e.g. 'Sftwr Engineering I:Principles'). Credit totals match the map exactly: terms 15+15+15+16+15+16+15+13 = 120 = the map's printed PROGRAM TOTALS of 120 (General Education 42; Major & Major Elective 65; Open Elective 13), equal to the catalog 120-credit degree minimum — no discrepancy. MATH 201 (Precalculus) is classified as a Major course per the map's printed Y1-Spring totals (9 GE / 6 Maj): it is the second major course alongside CISC 131. The map prints MATH 201's prerequisite as 'MATH 116 or B in HS algebra' — a placement alternative; the prereq points to MATH 116 (the in-plan course) and the 'B in high school algebra' placement option is documented here. The map's 'C or Higher' entries are grade milestones, not prerequisites, and are not encoded as prereqs. Markers: GC = Gateway Course (CISC 131, CISC 231); WBE = Work-Based Experience (CISC 380, CISC 381); CA/ELC = Career Activity / Experiential Learning Course (CISC 471). The three Mercy Seminars have no published course codes in any official Mercy sequence map (CS and Nursing 2026-2027 maps both omit them); descriptive placeholder codes MERCY-SEM-1/2/3 are used. ENGL 111/112 titled 'English Composition I/II' per the same-catalog-year official Mercy Nursing sequence map (the CS map abbreviates them as 'Comp 1'/'Comp II'; course codes are identical). ENGL 110 named in the Y1-Fall Gen Ed choice appears only as a choice option, not as a required course.",
